Subject: [PATCH] Clear scan_res_handler when an interface is disabled

A D-Bus Scan() call with AllowRoam=false queues the scan as radio work
and then sets wpa_s->scan_res_handler to scan_only_handler. If the
interface is disabled before that work starts, EVENT_INTERFACE_DISABLED
removes it with radio_remove_works(), and wpas_trigger_scan_cb() with
deinit set only frees the parameters of work that never started. The
handler stays set. The next scan on the interface, such as the one for
SelectNetwork(), then ends in "Scan-only results received", and
wpa_supplicant does not try to connect even though it found the network.

NetworkManager hits this when it switches from one network to another
with wifi.scan-rand-mac-address enabled, its default: it changes the
interface's address for scanning (down and up), calls Scan() with
AllowRoam=false, then restores the address for the new activation (down
again). If wpa_supplicant is still handling the first INTERFACE_ENABLED
when the second INTERFACE_DISABLED arrives, the queued scan is removed
before it starts, and NetworkManager fails the activation after 25 s.

Clear scan_res_handler along with the radio works on
EVENT_INTERFACE_DISABLED, as EVENT_SCAN_RESULTS already does for results
that arrive while the interface is disabled.

Not yet in hostap; carried by Sekka (DEVELOPERS.md, "Joining Wi-Fi
networks").
---
--- a/wpa_supplicant/events.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/events.c
@@ -7556,6 +7556,12 @@
 				       wpas_clear_disabled_interface,
 				       wpa_s, NULL);
 		radio_remove_works(wpa_s, NULL, 0);
+		/*
+		 * A scan removed here before it started never reports results.
+		 * Do not leave its handler, such as scan_only_handler for a
+		 * D-Bus Scan with AllowRoam=false, to take the next scan's.
+		 */
+		wpa_s->scan_res_handler = NULL;
 
 		wpa_supplicant_set_state(wpa_s, WPA_INTERFACE_DISABLED);
 		break;
